          "value": "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |",
