      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8590",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416 ) = 0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416 ) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/2be6ef2420c8789a0ff94f4f9540533af4134690ebe0c04c50eb02f358dfa266.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.8416) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le -0.8416) & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/example-8590.json",
